evidence.quote:
Prompt Optimization and Evolution

Automatic Prompt Optimization treats prompts as a black-box search over seeds, feedback, candidate generation and selection
(
Ramnath et al., 2025
)
.
Programmatic frameworks
(
Khattab et al., 2024
)
compile LM pipelines and optimize prompts offline using user metrics, while textual backpropagation
(
Yuksekgonul et al., 2025
;
Hu et al., 2024
;
Ma et al., 2025
)
utilizes natural-language feedback to refine collaboration protocols and behavioral instructions. Recent work jointly optimizes agentic structures and prompts
(
Tian et al., 2025
;
Murthy et al., 2025
;
Spiess et al., 2025
)
, using search-based strategies
(
Zhang et al., 2024
)
, genetic algorithms
(
Agrawal et al., 2026
)
and treats prompt optimization as experience-driven adaptation
(
Yao et al., 2022
;
Shinn et al., 2023
;
Zhao et al., 2024
;
Pei et al., 2025
;
Xie et al., 2026
)
.
